f unity and extraordinary  levels of  support so again we sometimes think of  contexts automatically changing human  behavior  no it's the way in which contexts are  understood  and made sense of it's the interaction  between the structure of experience and  leadership and the structure of rhetoric  which determines  outcomes it's not inevitable it's not  deterministic  it's the intersection of the political  and the psychological  which answers those questions well  uh that is uh all the time that we have  for today  unfortunately uh thank you to all who  are joining us from home and a huge  thank you to you  uh steven reicher for sharing your  insights with us  please visit our website at cfair.ca to  find out more about this  these series and to view a recording of  this talk which should be posted early  next week  could i make one final final point if i  may which is that the book  which we wrote we we  we wrote in order to be as uh broadly  available as possible so it is  available as a free download it doesn't  cost you anything you can buy it as a  paperback  but it's a free download so if you go to  look up together apart that's the name  of the book  um you can have it for free and you can  see some of the literature and the  evidence that lies behind some of the  things i've been saying  wonderful thanks so much steve thank you  you

